{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1448785-joint-fighting-merits","id":1448785,"title":"Joint Fighting Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-17T09:53:36-07:00","id":1448785,"title":"Joint Fighting Merits","content":"Are there any rules around fighting in a group? Like a duo or trio who fight together? Looking for merits or splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T11:10:37-07:00","id":1448788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghostdriver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1448785-joint-fighting-merits#post1448785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any rules around fighting in a group? Like a duo or trio who fight together? Looking for merits or splats.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Hunter: The Vigil </b>uses Tactics, which are sort of fancy Teamwork actions that let you take down monsters. That's the most obvious example I can think of, though there may be others. I don't know if there's anything more general than that, off the top of my head. Maybe check out <b>Hurt Locker</b>, which has a fair number of Fighting Styles and Physical Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T12:03:24-07:00","id":1448792,"title":"","content":"1e had Formation Tactics (Roman era shield walls) and Carthian Swarm (which really shouldn't be restricted to Carthians).<br /> <br /> 2e has drone, and two animal styles. These aren't quite the same thing, but worth looking atl. There's also the Cohesive Unit, Inspirational, and Small Unit Tactics Merits (the second two are mostly for commander types).<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken has a number of group fighting mechanics (mostly Merits) because... wolf packs and all that. The Pack supplement expands on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T15:40:10-07:00","id":1448810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1448785-joint-fighting-merits?p=1448792#post1448792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e had Formation Tactics (Roman era shield walls) and Carthian Swarm (which really shouldn't be restricted to Carthians).<br /> <br /> 2e has drone, and two animal styles. These aren't quite the same thing, but worth looking atl. There's also the Cohesive Unit, Inspirational, and Small Unit Tactics Merits (the second two are mostly for commander types).<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Forsaken has a number of group fighting mechanics (mostly Merits) because... wolf packs and all that. The Pack supplement expands on this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! Where do I find 'drone'? I'm looking to do something like a duo with another player. I am not set on any particular genre yet so anything in 2e would be great! Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T15:42:23-07:00","id":1448811,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker, sorry for not specifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T18:11:55-07:00","id":1448823,"title":"","content":"There aren't a lot of general merits that directly address fighting as a team (as mentioned Hunter and Werewolf have special options to emphasize those games' themes), but there are a handful that indirectly benefit teammates.<br /> <br /> Specifically: the third dot of Marksmanship from the Core protects allies from a missed shot into melee<br /> <br /> Between the Core and Hurt Locker there are a number of fighting merits that interact with the Prone tilt, making it easier to inflict or allowing you to do extra damage to prone opponents. The third dot of Street Fighting does both. The first dot of Grappling (Hurt Locker variant) and second (Core) both give you ways to render an opponent prone with grapple rolls, and the Ground and Pound maneuver (also Hurt Locker) gives you <i>rote </i>when attacking a downed enemy. <br /> <br /> Two or more characters with these merits could end fights very quickly by bypassing the usual drawback of needing to spend one turn to prone an opponent and then a second to perform the elbow drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}